{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useCanGoBack"},{"type":"text","value":" hook returns a boolean representing if the router history can safely go back without exiting the application."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"⚠️ The following new "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useCanGoBack"},{"type":"text","value":" API is currently "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"experimental"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"usecangoback-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useCanGoBack returns"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the router history is not at index "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the router history is at index "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"limitations","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limitations"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The router history index is reset after a navigation with "},{"type":"link","href":"./NavigateOptionsType.md#reloaddocument","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reloadDocument"}]},{"type":"text","value":" set as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":". This causes the router history to consider the new location as the initial one and will cause "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useCanGoBack"},{"type":"text","value":" to return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"false"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"showing-a-back-button","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Showing a back button"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useRouter, useCanGoBack } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const canGoBack = useCanGoBack()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {canGoBack ? (\n        <button onClick={() => router.history.back()}>Go back</button>\n      ) : null}\n\n      {/* ... */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"usecangoback-returns","text":"useCanGoBack returns","level":2},{"id":"limitations","text":"Limitations","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2},{"id":"showing-a-back-button","text":"Showing a back button","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThe `useCanGoBack` hook returns a boolean representing if the router history can safely go back without exiting the application.\n\n> ⚠️ The following new `useCanGoBack` API is currently _experimental_.\n\n## useCanGoBack returns\n\n- If the router history is not at index `0`, `true`.\n- If the router history is at index `0`, `false`.\n\n## Limitations\n\nThe router history index is reset after a navigation with [`reloadDocument`](./NavigateOptionsType.md#reloaddocument) set as `true`. This causes the router history to consider the new location as the initial one and will cause `useCanGoBack` to return `false`.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Showing a back button\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRouter, useCanGoBack } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const canGoBack = useCanGoBack()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {canGoBack ? (\n        <button onClick={() => router.history.back()}>Go back</button>\n      ) : null}\n\n      {/* ... */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: useCanGoBack\ntitle: useCanGoBack hook\n---\n\nThe `useCanGoBack` hook returns a boolean representing if the router history can safely go back without exiting the application.\n\n> ⚠️ The following new `useCanGoBack` API is currently _experimental_.\n\n## useCanGoBack returns\n\n- If the router history is not at index `0`, `true`.\n- If the router history is at index `0`, `false`.\n\n## Limitations\n\nThe router history index is reset after a navigation with [`reloadDocument`](./NavigateOptionsType.md#reloaddocument) set as `true`. This causes the router history to consider the new location as the initial one and will cause `useCanGoBack` to return `false`.\n\n## Examples\n\n### Showing a back button\n\n```tsx\nimport { useRouter, useCanGoBack } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nfunction Component() {\n  const router = useRouter()\n  const canGoBack = useCanGoBack()\n\n  return (\n    <div>\n      {canGoBack ? (\n        <button onClick={() => router.history.back()}>Go back</button>\n      ) : null}\n\n      {/* ... */}\n    </div>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
